  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered discovery comparisons are valid Welch analyses with adequate cell counts; estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For claim support I used the stated 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold and judged the signed lower bounds and point estimates. H45 and H46 reject the direct feature_037-by-feature_010 interaction. The signed estimates are tiny (+0.032 and -0.032) and the intervals include zero and substantial opposing uncertainty; this supports treating the two strong main associations as largely additive in this dataset rather than threshold-supported mutual modification. H129 through H132 accept conditional persistence of the central axes in partially constrained strata: feature_002 remains associated with higher outcome_001 when feature_037/feature_010 are constrained; feature_037 remains associated with lower outcome_001 when feature_002=1 and feature_010=0; and feature_010 remains associated with higher outcome_001 when feature_002=1 and feature_037=0. All signed lower bounds are far above 0.15, so despite multiplicity these are strong dataset-internal associations, though not proof of independent causal effects. H137 and H138 accept the cleaner joint-zero persistence tests: feature_010 remains positive and feature_037 remains negative when both feature_002 and the other central axis are zero, with lower bounds +0.302 and +0.768. These findings strengthen the central axis structure without implying adjustment for unmeasured confounders. The feature_010 assay-tail interaction screen now has a sharper boundary. H134 and H136 reject the strict one-sided attenuation tests in which the opposite standardized assay was constrained to be nonpositive. H134 (feature_018 high while feature_038<=0) is near null with signed point -0.014, and H136 (feature_038 positive while feature_018<=0) is also near null with signed point -0.054. Combined with accepted H117/H118/H119/H120/H122 and validated H110/H120, the evidence suggests attenuation of the feature_010 higher-outcome association is localized to positive or broadly nonnegative feature_038/feature_018 contexts, rather than to either high assay alone while the other is low or nonpositive. Because feature_038 and feature_018 are correlated constructed assays, this remains cross-assay tail heterogeneity and not a clean attribution to one assay. H139 and H140 reject feature_002-by-feature_038 tail interaction: H139 is opposite to the claimed direction and H140 is below threshold with a negative lower bound. This completes a largely negative assay-modification screen for feature_002 and supports interpreting feature_002 as a main higher-outcome/weaker-dependency axis rather than an assay-modified axis. I close H133 and H135 as unresolved/deferred strict opposite-tail tests because H134/H136 fail and the strict cells are likely sparse; further slots are better spent on nonnegative-context tests and validation. I request independent validation for H122 because it is a broad feature_038 attenuation interaction accepted on discovery, directly complements the validated broad feature_018 form H120, and would test whether the feature_038 attenuation pattern survives the run's stringent independent threshold. The newly registered follow-up proposals test one-sided nonnegative assay contexts (feature_018 attenuation among feature_038>=0 and feature_038 attenuation among feature_018>=0) and the absolute feature_010 effect inside the joint-positive feature_038>=0 and feature_018>=0 stratum. All conclusions remain dataset-internal associations; none establish causality, mechanism, gene-level biology, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 appraise. Central accepted axes unchanged: feature_037=1 lower outcome_001; feature_010=1 higher outcome_001; feature_002=1 higher outcome_001, all validated main effects. New accepted and closed conditional persistence: H129-H132 and joint-zero H137-H138. New rejected and closed: H45/H46 direct feature_037-feature_010 interaction; H134/H136 one-sided feature_010 tail attenuation when opposite assay nonpositive; H139/H140 feature_002-by-feature_038 interaction. H133/H135 closed unresolved because strict opposite-tail tests are sparse/low priority and broad one-sided nonpositive tests failed. Feature_010 attenuation now best interpreted as localized to joint/broad nonnegative feature_038/feature_018 assay structure, not to one assay alone; validated formulations are H110 (restricted high feature_038) and H120 (broad feature_018 excluding low feature_038). H122 is broad feature_038 attenuation under feature_018>=-1 and is the requested validation candidate. New proposals: interaction feature_010 with eligibility feature_038>=0 and subgroup feature_018>=0; mirror eligibility feature_018>=0 and subgroup feature_038>=0; and mean feature_010 difference in joint-positive eligibility to assess residual absolute effect. Do not overinterpret accepted subgroup means for feature_037 or feature_002 as interaction evidence; their direct tail interactions failed. Continue to treat all statements as dataset-internal associations without causal, mechanistic, gene-level, or generalizable claims.",
